iabilities to all other foreigners, which are used in the U.S. balance of payments statistics.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 288, 1503, 377], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-3 shows nonmarketable bonds and notes that Treasury issues to official institutions and other residents of foreign countries.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 382, 1497, 632], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-4, which presented a trade-weighted index of the foreign currency value of the dollar, has been discontinued. The \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" first published an index of effective exchange rate changes for the dollar, as Table IFS-7, in June 1974. In the intervening time, many other indices have been developed that are widely accepted indicators of general movement of the dollar. The index presented in IFS-4 used a simple functional form and publicly available information so that the index can be easily replicated by those who find it useful.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [574, 653, 1058, 684], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"TABLE IFS-1.--U.S. Reserve Assets\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 684, 1078, 714], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Office of International Financial Analysis]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [120, 714, 1515, 1789], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>End of calendar year or month</th><th>Total reserve assets<sup>1</sup> (1)</th><th>Gold stock<sup>2</sup> (2)</th><th>Special drawing rights<sup>1,3</sup> (3)</th><th>Foreign currencies<sup>4</sup> (4)</th><th>Reserve position in International Monetary Fund<sup>1,5</sup> (5)</th></tr><tr><td>1991</td><td>77,721</td><td>11,059</td><td>11,240</td><td>45,934</td><td>9,488</td></tr><tr><td>1992</td><td>71,323</td><td>11,056</td><td>8,503</td><td>40,005</td><td>11,759</td></tr><tr><td>1993</td><td>73,442</td><td>11,053</td><td>9,039</td><td>41,532</td><td>11,818</td></tr><tr><td>1994</td><td>74,335</td><td>11,051</td><td>10,039</td><td>41,215</td><td>12,030</td></tr><tr><td>1995 -Apr.</td><td>88,756</td><td>11,055</td><td>11,743</td><td>51,752</td><td>14,206</td></tr><tr><td>May</td><td>90,549</td><td>11,054</td><td>11,923</td><td>53,294</td><td>14,278</td></tr><tr><td>June</td><td>90,063</td><td>11,054</td><td>11,869</td><td>52,864</td><td>14,276</td></tr><tr><td>July</td><td>91,534</td><td>11,053</td><td>11,487</td><td>54,233</td><td>14,761</td></tr><tr><td>Aug.</td><td>86,648</td><td>11,053</td><td>11,146</td><td>49,979</td><td>14,470</td></tr><tr><td>Sept.</td><td>87,152</td><td>11,051</td><td>11,035</td><td>50,385</td><td>14,681</td></tr><tr><td>Oct.</td><td>86,224</td><td>11,051</td><td>10,949</td><td>49,524</td><td>14,700</td></tr><tr><td>Nov.</td><td>85,755</td><td>11,050</td><td>11,034</td><td>49,099</td><td>14,572</td></tr><tr><td>Dec.</td><td>85,832</td><td>11,050</td><td>11,037</td><td>49,096</td><td>14,649</td></tr><tr><td>1996 -Jan.</td><td>82,717</td><td>11,052</td><td>10,778</td><td>46,575</td><td>14,312</td></tr><tr><td>Feb.</td><td>84,270</td><td>11,053</td><td>11,106</td><td>47,298</td><td>14,813</td></tr><tr><td>Mar.</td><td>84,212</td><td>11,053</td><td>11,049</td><td>46,861</td><td>15,249</td></tr><tr><td>Apr.</td><td>83,710</td><td>11,052</td><td>10,963</td><td>46,578</td><td>15,117</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 1796, 814, 1940], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"1 Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) adopted a technique for valuing the special drawing right (SDR) based on a weighted-average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and reserve position in the IMF are also valued on this basis beginning July 1974.\\na Treasury values its gold stock at $42,222 per fine troy ounce and pursuant to 31 U.S.C. 5117\\nb issues gold certificates to the Federal Reserve at the same rate against all gold held.\\n3 Includes allocations of SDRs in the Special Drawing Account in the IMF, plus or minus transactions in SDRs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1789, 1510, 1900], \"page_id\": 65}], \"content\": \"4 Includes holdings of Treasury and Federal Reserve System; beginning November 1978, these are valued at current market exchange rates or, where appropriate, at such other rates as may be agreed upon by the parties to the transactions.\\n5 The United States has the right to purchase foreign currencies equivalent to its reserve position in the IMF automatically if needed. Under appropriate conditions, the United States could purchase additional amounts related to the U.S. quota.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 87, 173, 108], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"64\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 90, 1091, 111], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"INTERNATIONAL FINANCIAL STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [474, 196, 1158, 231], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"TABLE IFS-2.--Selected U.S. Liabilities to Foreigners\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [568, 233, 1067, 255], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: Office of International Financial Analysis)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 273, 1503, 1704], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>End of calendar year or month</th><th>Total (1)</th><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Official institutions<sup>1</sup></th><th colspan=\