 purchases on an annual basis for 1992 through 1995, and on a year-to-date basis for 1996. The figures show that there has been overall a steady increase in foreigners' net purchases, or gross purchases minus gross sales, of U.S. securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [244, 1751, 809, 1817], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"On an annualized basis, net purchases by foreigners accelerated in the first quarter of 1996 for all\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1431, 1393, 1787], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"regions shown except the United Kingdom and the Caribbean banking centers. Net purchases opposite Japan in the first quarter were vigorous compared to 1995, but still lagged behind the high pace of net purchases in 1994. After peaking at $100 billion in 1995, net purchases opposite the United Kingdom slackened somewhat in the first quarter, but remained strong. The only substantial reversal occurred opposite the Caribbean banking centers, which saw a year of very robust acquisitions followed by a large sell-off of U.S. securities, or negative net purchases, in the first quarter of 1996.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [665, 94, 974, 130], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"CAPITAL MOVEMENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1454, 99, 1492, 130], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"91\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 193, 1475, 271], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"SECTION V.--Transactions in Long-Term Securities by Foreigners Reported by Banks and Brokers in the United States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [226, 295, 1406, 337], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"TABLE CM-V-1.--Foreign Purchases and Sales of Long-Term Domestic Securities by