e table ESF-2)</td><td>24,833,301</td><td>-104,526</td><td>24,728,775</td></tr><tr><td>Total capital</td><td>25,033,301</td><td>-104,526</td><td>24,928,775</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities and capital</td><td>42,635,897</td><td>-204,161</td><td>42,431,736</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1898, 401, 1921], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"See footnotes on the following page.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 92, 195, 130], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"106\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [590, 92, 1044, 130], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"EXCHANGE STABILIZATION FUND\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [541, 184, 1096, 240], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"TABLE ESF-2.\\u2014Income and Expense\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 252, 1082, 285], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars. Source: Office of the Secretary of the Treasury)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 285, 1497, 1065], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Income and expense</th><th>Current quarter<br>Oct. 1, 1995, through Dec. 31, 1995</th><th>Fiscal year to date<br>Oct. 1, 1995, through Dec. 31, 1995</th></tr><tr><td>Profit (loss) on:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>-449,353</td><td>-449,353</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations 1</td><td>-49,225</td><td>-49,225</td></tr><tr><td>Interest (net charges) on:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Special drawing rights</td><td>39,840</td><td>39,840</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>37,892</td><td>37,892</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>316,320</td><td>316,320</td></tr><tr><td>Income from operations</td><td>-104,526</td><td>-104,526</td></tr><tr><td>Net income (loss)</td><td>-104,526</td><td>-104,526</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 1096, 801, 1197], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"1 Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) adopted a technique for valuing the special drawing rights (SDRs) based on a weighted average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and allocations are valued on this basis beginning July 1974. 2 Excludes foreign exchange transactions for future and spot delivery.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 1096, 1499, 1188], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Annual balance sheets for fiscal years 1934 through 1940 appeared in the 1940 \\\"Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury\\\" and those for succeeding years appeared in subsequent reports through 1980. Quarterly balance sheets for beginning with Dec. 31, 1938, have been published in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\" Data from inception to Sept. 30, 1978, may be found on the statements published in the January 1979 \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1408, 82, 1472, 113], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"107\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [536, 717, 1133, 759], \"page_id\": 109}], \"content\": \"Page Intentionally Left Blank\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 87, 242, 118], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"108\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 714, 1133, 761], \"page_id\": 110}], \"content\": \"Page Intentionally Left Blank\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 97, 911, 127], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1441, 97, 1490, 127], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"109\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [388, 196, 1239, 238], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 283, 798, 516], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"The Airport and Airway Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1971, according to provisions of the Airport and Airway Revenue Act of 1970 [49 U.S.C. 1742 (a)]. The trust fund was re-established in the Internal Revenue Code (26 U.S.C. 9502) as a result of the Tax Equity and Fiscal Responsibility Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-248, dated September 3, 1982), effective September 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 516, 796, 742], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Amounts equivalent to the taxes received in the Treasury on transportation of persons and property by air, gasoline and jet fuel used in noncommercial aircraft, and an international departure tax are appropriated from the general fund of the Treasury to the trust fund. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) increased rates for the excise taxes transferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 745, 796, 837], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"These transfers are made based on estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury, subject to adjustments in later transfers in the amount of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 285, 1490, 460], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 U.S.C. 9602 (b) are met, amounts available in the fund exceeding outlay requirements are invested in public debt securities with the interest credited to the fund. Additional sums from the general fund are also credited as authorized and made available by law, if necessary, to meet outlay requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 462, 1490, 547], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Amounts required for outlays to carry out the airport and airway program are made available to the Federal Aviation Administration, Department of Transportation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 547, 1492, 660], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Other charges to the trust fund are made by the Secretary of the Treasury for transfers of certain refunds of taxes and certain outfits under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 662, 1492, 837], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Transportation. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 863, 1155, 933], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-10.\\u2014Airport and Airway Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1995\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [665, 957, 964, 981], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 981, 1490, 1907], \"page_id\": 111}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Descriptio