id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 255, 1492, 410], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"12-month revenue estimates for the highway and mass transit accounts, respectively, include the latest estimates received from the Department of Treasury's Office of Tax Analysis for excise taxes, net of refunds. They represent net highway receipts for those periods beginning at the close of fiscal 1995.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [688, 481, 944, 521], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"Highway Account\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [592, 544, 1042, 570], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 582, 1494, 665], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Unfunded authorizations (EOY)</td><td>39,253</td></tr><tr><td>24-month revenue estimate.</td><td>45,818</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [661, 695, 969, 731], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"Mass Transit Account\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [592, 757, 1040, 783], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 794, 1494, 877], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Unfunded authorizations (EOY)</td><td>4,938</td></tr><tr><td>12-month revenue estimate</td><td>3,640</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 99, 913, 127], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1444, 97, 1490, 130], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"117\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [401, 196, 1229, 240], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Inland Waterways Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 283, 794, 547], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The Inland Waterways Trust Fund was established by the Treasury in fiscal 1984, according to provisions of the Inland Waterways Revenue Act of 1978 (Public Law 95-502) and continued according to the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (26 U.S.C. 9506). Amounts determined by the Secretary of the Treasury to be section 4042 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 (relating to tax on fuel used in commercial transportation on Inland Waterways) shall be appropriated to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 547, 796, 719], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The Technical and Miscellaneous Revenue Act of 1988 (Public Law 100-647, approved November 10, 1988) increased the tax each year, 1990 through 1995. These amounts are transferred quarterly from the general fund based on estimates made by the Secretary, subject to adjustments in later transfers to the amounts of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 717, 796, 778], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Treasury invests in interest-bearing obligations of the United States that portion of the trust fund,\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 283, 1490, 547], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"in his judgment, not required to meet current withdrawals. The interest on, and proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligation held in the trust fund is credited to the trust fund. The act provides that amounts in the trust fund shall be available, by appropriations acts, for making construction and rehabilitation expenditures for navigation on the inland and intracoastal waterways of the United States described in 33 U.S.C. 1804. Expenditures must be otherwise authorized by law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 544, 1492, 721], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [484, 849, 1148, 919], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-16.\\u2014Inland Waterways Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1995\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [670, 945, 960, 969], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"[Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 983, 1497, 1299], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1994</td><td>$214,313,309</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fuel taxes</td><td>103,416,030</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>15,580,324</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>118,996,354</td></tr><tr><td>Transfers:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>94,777,965</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1995</td><td>238,531,698</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [495, 1313, 1129, 1381], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations Fiscal Years 1996-2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [740, 1410, 891, 1433], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"(In millions o