{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377883-VV5uDcIZKcFUmS7yxeE8","role":"assistant","created":1775377894,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I found the exact data. From TABLE CM-I-2 (Total Liabilities by Type, Payable in Dollars - Part A: Foreign Countries):\n\n- 1991: 747,085 million dollars\n- 1992: 800,909 million dollars\n- 1993: 915,736 million dollars\n- 1994: 1,006,151 million dollars\n\nThe question asks for the Total Liabilities (all types combined) for Foreign Countries for years 1991 through 1996. Let me verify by checking if the data I found is exactly what's asked.\n\nActually wait - the question says \"Total Liabilities (all types combined)\" - this would be the Grand Total (both dollars and foreign currencies), not just the \"payable in dollars\" column.\n\nLooking at CM-I-1, I found:\n- 1991: 831,195 (Total liabilities)\n- 1992: 883,055\n- 1993: 1,004,931\n- 1994: 1,104,041\n\nBut I need to separate Foreign Countries from International and Regional. The question asks specifically for \"Foreign Countries\".\n\nLet me recalculate:\n- From CM-I-1: Total liabilities includes both Foreign countries and International/regional\n- From CM-I-2: Part A shows Foreign Countries with breakdown by type (deposits, treasury bills, etc.)\n- The question says \"Total Liabilities (all types combined)\" - this would be the total in millions\n\nLooking at the first row of CM-I-2 for foreign countries:\n- 1991: 747,085 (payable in dollars)\n- 1992: 800,909\n- 1993: 915,736\n- 1994: 1,006,151\n\nWait, this is \"payable in dollars\" only. What about foreign currencies?\n\nLooking at CM-I-1:\n- 1991: Total Foreign Countries = 831,195 - 9,252 (international) = 821,943\n\n\n- I need to verify the exact figure for foreign countries\n\nI'm carefully examining the table structure. The data in CM-I-1 shows total liabilities but doesn't clearly separate foreign countries. I'll need to cross-reference the columns to confirm the precise total for foreign countries.\