{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377904-Wc1NU9UL59JUVH0dJTdR","role":"assistant","created":1775377914,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the CM-I-1 table from the 1997 bulletin, I can see the calendar years:\n- 1992: Total = 883055 (total liabilities)\n- 1993: Total = 1004931\n- 1994: Total = 1104254\n- 1995: Total = 1209262\n- 1996: Dec = 1241557\n\nSo for Foreign Countries Total Liabilities (all types combined) for calendar years:\n- 1992: Need to find the value in the \"Foreign countries\" column\n- 1993: Need to find the value\n- 1994: Need to find the value\n- 1995: Need to find the value\n- 1996: Need to find the value\n\nActually, wait - I need to look at the CM-I-1 data which shows \"Total foreign countries\" not \"Total liabilities\". Let me check the columns more carefully.\n\nLooking at the table, I see columns:\n- Total liabilities (1)\n- Official institutions 1 - Total (2)\n- Official institutions 1 - Payable in dollars (3)\n- Banks and other foreigners - Payable in foreign currencies 3 (4)\n- Banks and other foreigners - Total (5)\n- International and regional 2 - Payable in dollars (6)\n- International and regional 2 - Payable in foreign currencies 3 (7)\n- etc.\n\nThe \"Total liabilities (1)\" is the Grand total, not just foreign countries.\n\nTo get \"Total foreign countries\" (all types combined), I need to add:\n- Official institutions Total (column 2)\n- Banks and other foreigners Total (column 5)\n- International and regional Total\n\nOr more simply, from the CM-I-2 table (Part A), I found earlier which has \"Total foreign countries (1)\" column.\n\nLooking at the earlier data I extracted from CM-I-2 in the 1996 bulletin:\n- 1991: 747085\n\n\n- 1992: 800909\n- 1993: 915736\n- 1994: 1006151\n\nNow I need to locate 1995 and 1996 data. Checking the 1997 bulletin should give me access to those figures. From what I observed in CM-I-3, the Total foreign countries for December shows 1226029.0 for 1996.\n\nLooking at the available data, I can pull together the foreign country totals across years: 1991 comes from CM-I-2 at 747085, while 1992 through 1994 are 800909, 915736, and 1006151 respectively from the same source. The 1995 figure appears to be 1197085 based on the CM-I-3 table in the 1996 bulletin, and 1996 is partially visible at 1196034.0.\n\nChecking the 1997 bulletin confirms 1995 at 1197085.0 and shows 1996 at 1241557 (December figure). Since the question specifies calendar years 1991 through 1996, I need the full year values, and 1996 data from the 1997 bulletin gives me the complete year at 1241557. The earlier partial 1996 figure of 1196034.0 in the 1996 bulletin was only through November.\n\nLooking at the available documents, 1991 is only present in the 1996 bulletin through CM-I-2 as 747085. The remaining years check out: 1992 (800909), 1993 (915736), 1994 (1006151), 1995 (1197085), and 1996 (1241557). With all six years accounted for, I can now compute the arithmetic mean across the period.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ac459b3a96584a55ae114641","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1998_06.txt | grep -A 30 \"TABLE CM-I-1\" | head -35"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
